  "domain": "infer-core",
  "level": "L2",
  "title": "Receiver closure is observed at batch boundaries, and cleanup calls can still fail",
  "mechanism": "TGI v2 drops queued requests with closed response receivers and removes stopped entries after a prefill/decode result is dispatched. The current RPC is not explicitly preempted by those checks. filter_batch uses cardinality equality as a shortcut; otherwise it filters request IDs or clears the shard cache. In prefill/decode error handlers, cache cleanup is attempted and its Result is discarded before errors are sent to all affected entries.",
  "corrections": [
    "Replace statements that error cleanup succeeds with 'attempts clear_cache'; backend.rs:271 and 315-318 discard cleanup errors.",
    "State that request-ID equality is an assumed invariant behind the size shortcut, not a demonstrated runtime bug.",
    "build_server(false) concerns generated bindings only; it does not establish absence of server code elsewhere.",
    "queue.rs contains unit-test source; no tests were executed in this review.",
    "Additional source-level caveat: queue.rs:240-274 mutates token totals before rejecting an over-budget entry; batch.max_tokens at 334-338 can include that rejected entry when earlier entries remain. No throughput impact was measured."
  ],
  "source_scope": "Corrected runtime ranges read; test module presence checked, test suite not run.",
